  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "Continuous networks G_theta(z) trained under minibatch OT or relativistic critic losses fail on disconnected multimodal targets for four coupled structural reasons: (1) when inter-mode distances exceed the unbalanced screening horizon (img_bars4 c_hat~44 >> rho=3) or minibatch size falls below mode count (grid100 B=64 < M=100), empty modes dump into slack while 52.5% of settled grid modes suffer false minibatch-absence critic kicks and soft Sinkhorn averages cross-valley pulls into 0.5-ghosts; persistent multi-batch chart accumulation (K<=256) with Laguerre hard Monge commitment and C^1 halo dead-zone eliminates 0.5-ghosts and false kicks with zero intra-mode shrinkage; (2) global scalar horizons lock onto narrow modes and falsely eject wide modes (vector_unequal_width 0.07..0.30); symmetric conformal local horizons ell(u,v)=sqrt(ell_tilde(u)*ell_tilde(v)) preserve exact zero Feydy self-coupling bias while scaling linearly per mode; (3) post-LeakyReLU generator layer activations share DC/correlated components across modes; whitened polar steps polar(G_W P_tilde) P_tilde deconflict shared weights; (4) hollow conditional IMQ-CMMD saturates on cross-context mean drift (model_ddgan_gaussian_chain t1_q0); pair-swap-invariant midpoint ridge drift subtraction restores quadratic kernel curvature with exact zero finite-sample bias.",
